IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp5-months`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division D (Payment of Benefits: Special Rules Applicable)
-- REINSTATEMENT OF A DISABILITY PENSION OR POST-RETIREMENT DISABILITY BENEFIT: section 70.1.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- A person who left a disability pension (or post-retirement disability benefit) to return to work may have it
-- reinstated if they become incapable of working again within two years. The Minister's satisfaction (paragraph
-- (3)(a): the disability is the same as, or related to, the earlier one) is a plain input; the dates and the age
-- are worked out from facts. Regulation 71(2) (the Regulations, piece cr2) fixes the time for the request; it is
-- read here so that the question "am I in time?" has an answer, and cr2 encodes the regulation itself.
-- A month is the DATE of its first day.

-- out of range: paragraph 42(2)(a) (piece cp3): "severe and prolonged" disability, the Minister's judgment in s 70.1(3)(a), a plain input
-- out of range: subsection 45(2) (piece cp3): the annual adjustment of the amount in s 70.1(9), a plain input
-- out of range: paragraph 44(1)(e) and subsection 42(1) (piece cp3): the child's requirements for a disabled contributor's child benefit, a plain input in s 70.1(4)
-- out of range: subsections 60(2), (4), (5) and (8) to (12) (piece cp4): they apply to the request with the modifications the circumstances require; not modelled
-- out of range: regulation 71 (piece cr2): read in s 70.1(2)

§ `Part II, Division D -- Reinstatement of a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit (section 70.1)`

§§ `Subsection 70.1(1) -- the entitlement`

-- src:2319 | Reinstatement of disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit
-- src:2320 | 70.1 (1) Subject to this section, a person who has ceased to receive a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit because they have returned to work is entitled to have that pension or benefit reinstated if, within two years after the month in which they ceased to receive it, they become incapable again of working.
@ref Act s 70.1(1) (src:2320)
GIVEN `the person ceased to receive the pension or benefit because they returned to work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(1) — the person is entitled to have the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit reinstated` `the person ceased to receive the pension or benefit because they returned to work` `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` MEANS
        `the person ceased to receive the pension or benefit because they returned to work`
    AND `cp5 helper -- the number of months from the month the person ceased to receive it to the month they became incapable again` `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` AT LEAST 0
    AND `cp5 helper -- the number of months from the month the person ceased to receive it to the month they became incapable again` `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` AT MOST 24

-- Subsection (1) says "within two years after the month in which they ceased to receive it"; paragraph (3)(b) says
-- "not more than two years have elapsed from the month in which the person ceased ... to the month when they became
-- incapable again". Both count whole months from the month of ceasing to the month of the new incapacity;
-- the same month counts as 0 and a month before the ceasing is not "again" (NOTES.md, fork F18).
GIVEN ceased IS A DATE
      incapable IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp5 helper -- the number of months from the month the person ceased to receive it to the month they became incapable again` ceased incapable MEANS
    `the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` ceased incapable

§§ `Subsection 70.1(2) -- the request`

-- src:2321 | Request for reinstatement
-- src:2322 | (2) A request by a person for reinstatement of a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit shall be made to the Minister in accordance with the regulations. Subsections 60(2), (4), (5) and (8) to (12) apply to the request, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref Act s 70.1(2) (src:2322)
-- The Act says the request is made "in accordance with the regulations". Regulation 71 is the Regulations' Request
-- for Reinstatement (piece cr2): writing, to the Minister, within 12 months after the month the person became
-- incapable again of working.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:707 | 71 (1) A request for reinstatement of a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit under section 70.1 of the Act shall be made by submitting it to the Minister in writing.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:708 | (2) The request shall be made within 12 months after the month in which the person became incapable again of working.
@ref Act s 70.1(2); Reg 71 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:707-708)
GIVEN `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` IS A DATE
      `day the request was made` IS A DATE
      `the request was made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(2) — the request for reinstatement was made in accordance with the regulations` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` `day the request was made` `the request was made in writing to the Minister` MEANS
        `the request was made in writing to the Minister`
    -- within 12 months after the month in which the person became incapable again: through the end of the twelfth
    -- month after that month (NOTES.md, fork F10)
    AND `day the request was made` BELOW `the month following the month of a date` (`cp5 helper -- the month a number of months from the month of a date` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` 12)

§§ `Subsection 70.1(3) -- the Minister shall approve the request`

-- src:2323 | Consideration and approval of request by Minister
-- src:2324 | (3) The Minister shall approve a request made by a person under subsection (2) if the Minister is satisfied that
-- src:2325 | (a) the person has a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or is related to, the disability that entitled the person to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that is the subject of the request;
-- src:2326 | (b) not more than two years have elapsed from the month in which the person ceased to receive the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit to the month when they became incapable again of working; and
-- src:2327 | (c) the person had not reached 65 years of age and, if the request is for reinstatement of a disability pension, was not receiving a retirement pension in the month in which they became incapable again of working.
@ref Act s 70.1(3) (src:2324-2327)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the person has a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or related to, the earlier disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the request is for reinstatement of a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was receiving a retirement pension in the month they became incapable again of working` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(3) — the Minister must approve the request for reinstatement` `the Minister is satisfied that the person has a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or related to, the earlier disability` `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` `date of birth` `the request is for reinstatement of a disability pension` `the person was receiving a retirement pension in the month they became incapable again of working` MEANS
    -- (a) the same or a related severe and prolonged disability
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability that is the same as, or related to, the earlier disability`
    -- (b) not more than two years have elapsed from the month the person ceased to receive it to the month they became incapable again
    AND `cp5 helper -- the number of months from the month the person ceased to receive it to the month they became incapable again` `a day in the month the person ceased to receive it` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` AT MOST 24
    -- (c) the person had not reached 65 and, if the request is for a disability pension, was not receiving a retirement pension
    --     in the month they became incapable again of working
    AND (NOT (`cp5 helper -- the person has reached an age on a day under section 2(2)` `date of birth` 65 `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working`))
    AND (   (NOT `the request is for reinstatement of a disability pension`)
         OR (NOT `the person was receiving a retirement pension in the month they became incapable again of working`))

§§ `Subsection 70.1(4) -- the disabled contributor's child's benefit`

-- src:2328 | Reinstatement of disabled contributor’s child benefit
-- src:2329 | (4) On reinstatement of a pension or benefit under subsection (3), the Minister shall approve the reinstatement of a disabled contributor’s child benefit that had been payable to the child of the person whose pension or benefit is reinstated if the Minister is satisfied that the child meets the requirements under this Act for payment of a disabled contributor’s child benefit.
@ref Act s 70.1(4) (src:2329)
GIVEN `the pension or benefit is reinstated under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the child meets the requirements under this Act for payment of a disabled contributor's child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(4) — the Minister must approve the reinstatement of the disabled contributor's child benefit` `the pension or benefit is reinstated under subsection (3)` `the Minister is satisfied that the child meets the requirements under this Act for payment of a disabled contributor's child benefit` MEANS
        `the pension or benefit is reinstated under subsection (3)`
    AND `the Minister is satisfied that the child meets the requirements under this Act for payment of a disabled contributor's child benefit`

§§ `Subsections 70.1(5) and (6) -- the Minister informs in writing`

-- src:2330 | Notification of decision — disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit
-- src:2331 | (5) The Minister shall in writing inform a person who makes the request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit of the Minister’s decision whether or not to approve the request.
@ref Act s 70.1(5) (src:2331)
GIVEN `the person made a request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(5) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve the request` `the person made a request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit` MEANS
    `the person made a request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit`

-- src:2332 | Notification of decision — disabled contributor’s child benefit
-- src:2333 | (6) The Minister shall in writing inform the person who has made the request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit, a child of that person or, in relation to that child, a person or agency referred to in section 75 of the Minister’s decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor’s child benefit.
@ref Act s 70.1(6) (src:2333)
-- out of range: section 75 (this piece): the person or agency who has decision-making responsibility for the child
GIVEN `the person made the request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a child of the person who made the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or agency is referred to in section 75 in relation to that child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(6) — the Minister must inform the person in writing of the decision whether or not to approve a disabled contributor's child benefit` `the person made the request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit` `the person is a child of the person who made the request` `the person or agency is referred to in section 75 in relation to that child` MEANS
        `the person made the request for reinstatement of a pension or benefit`
     OR `the person is a child of the person who made the request`
     OR `the person or agency is referred to in section 75 in relation to that child`

§§ `Subsections 70.1(7) and (8) -- which provisions apply to the reinstated pension or benefit`

-- The provisions that the two subsections except. The pension, benefit or child's benefit that is reinstated is
-- governed by every other provision of the Act that applies to it, "with any modifications that the circumstances require".
-- src:2334 | Application of provisions — reinstated pension or benefit
-- src:2335 | (7) The provisions of this Act that apply to a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit, as the case may be, except paragraphs 42(2)(b), 44(1)(b) and (h) and (2)(a) and subsection 44(4) and sections 69 and 70.01, apply to a pension or benefit that is reinstated under this section, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
-- src:2336 | Application of provisions — disabled contributor’s child benefit
-- src:2337 | (8) The provisions of this Act that apply to a disabled contributor’s child benefit, except paragraphs 44(1)(e) and 44(2)(a) and subsections 44(4) and 74(2), apply to a disabled contributor’s child benefit that is reinstated under this section, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
@ref Act s 70.1(7), s 70.1(8) (src:2335-2337)
DECLARE `cp5 Provision of the Act that section 70.1 may except` IS ONE OF
    `the provision paragraph 42(2)(b)`
    `the provision paragraph 44(1)(b)`
    `the provision paragraph 44(1)(e)`
    `the provision paragraph 44(1)(h)`
    `the provision paragraph 44(2)(a)`
    `the provision subsection 44(4)`
    `the provision subsection 74(2)`
    `the provision section 69`
    `the provision section 70.01`
    `another provision of the Act`

@ref Act s 70.1(7) (src:2335)
GIVEN provision IS A `cp5 Provision of the Act that section 70.1 may except`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(7) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `the provision paragraph 42(2)(b)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision paragraph 44(1)(b)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision paragraph 44(1)(h)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision paragraph 44(2)(a)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision subsection 44(4)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision section 69` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision section 70.01` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref Act s 70.1(8) (src:2337)
GIVEN provision IS A `cp5 Provision of the Act that section 70.1 may except`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 70.1(8) — a provision of the Act applies to a reinstated disabled contributor's child benefit` provision MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `the provision paragraph 44(1)(e)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision paragraph 44(2)(a)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision subsection 44(4)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the provision subsection 74(2)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Subsection 70.1(9) -- the least amount`

-- src:2338 | Amount of disability pension and survivor’s pension
-- src:2339 | (9) Despite subsection (7) and subject to any division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under sections 55 to 55.3, the basic monthly amount of a disability pension that is reinstated, and the monthly amount of any survivor’s pension under this Act that is payable to the person whose disability pension is reinstated, shall not be less than the amount that was payable for the month immediately preceding the month in which the pension ceased to be payable, adjusted annually in accordance with subsection 45(2).
@ref Act s 70.1(9) (src:2339)
-- out of range: subsection 45(2) (piece cp3): the amount payable for the month before the pension ceased, adjusted
-- annually; and the amount the rules of Division B give without this subsection
GIVEN `the amount calculated under the rules of Part II without this subsection` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount payable for the month immediately preceding the month the pension ceased, adjusted annually in accordance with subsection 45(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under sections 55 to 55.3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 70.1(9) — the monthly amount of the reinstated disability pension, or of the survivor's pension payable to the person` `the amount calculated under the rules of Part II without this subsection` `the amount payable for the month immediately preceding the month the pension ceased, adjusted annually in accordance with subsection 45(2)` `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under sections 55 to 55.3 applies` MEANS
    IF `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under sections 55 to 55.3 applies`
    -- "subject to any division of unadjusted pensionable earnings": the division prevails over the floor (NOTES.md, fork F11)
    THEN `the amount calculated under the rules of Part II without this subsection`
    ELSE IF `the amount calculated under the rules of Part II without this subsection` AT LEAST `the amount payable for the month immediately preceding the month the pension ceased, adjusted annually in accordance with subsection 45(2)`
         THEN `the amount calculated under the rules of Part II without this subsection`
         ELSE `the amount payable for the month immediately preceding the month the pension ceased, adjusted annually in accordance with subsection 45(2)`

§§ `Subsection 70.1(10) -- when payment begins`

-- src:2340 | Commencement of payments
-- src:2341 | (10) A disability pension, post-retirement disability benefit or disabled contributor’s child benefit that is reinstated pursuant to a request under this section is payable commencing with the month following the month in which the person who made the request under this section became incapable again of working.
@ref Act s 70.1(10) (src:2341)
GIVEN `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 70.1(10) — the month with which a reinstated pension or benefit is payable` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` `a day in the month the person became incapable again of working`
